From 8534232d26d0e96f8c03ecbc936cb9b28ce3146d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dnz3d4c <dnz3d4c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:33:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Korean: the mod's own strings, generated from the
 catalogue
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The subject stays put on purpose - this one commit holds every translated
string and grows with each feature group, so the patch file keeps its name
instead of being renamed on every batch.

Generated, not written. The Korean here comes from overlay/ko/ko.json through
tools/ko-apply; this C# is output. Do not hand-edit it, and do not resolve
conflicts in it - drop the commit and run the tool again against the new tree.

That is the point of the commit. Korean has to land on 688 lines of a file
upstream touches in nearly every release, and upstream released seven times in
eight days. A hand-written diff of that size would have to be re-merged by hand
on that cadence, by someone reading the diff with a screen reader. Regenerating
is deterministic; merging is not. The failure mode becomes "N strings in the
catalogue are no longer in the source", which names the sentence that moved.

669 strings on 686 of the 688 call sites - everything the tool can reach.
The mod now speaks Korean end to end: menus, navigation, combat, hotbars,
crafting, gathering, loot rolls, the deep dungeon, character creation and the
chat group.

Game words are the game's own, read out of the Korean client's Addon sheet
rather than guessed (tools/ko-terms; overlay/ko/terms.json records the row
number for each). A few that guessing would have got wrong:

- The game has no word "채팅" - zero hits across all 19,592 Addon rows. It
  says 로그 for the log and 대화 for conversation
- Echo is 혼잣말, and the loot-roll trio is 선입찰 / 입찰 / 포기 (Addon 390-392)
- The Hunting Log is 토벌수첩 and a hunting target is 토벌 대상 (1880, 8425)
- Minions are 꼬마 친구 (4902) and retainers 집사 (532)

A review pass over all 686 sites moved 37 of them. What it caught, and why the
first pass could not:

- Words that are not the client's. The game's inventory is 소지품 (520); 가방
  is the chocobo saddlebag (880-892). The Hand Over button is 건네주기 (88).
  The mailbox is 편지함 (1807), the Hall of the Novice 초보자의 집 (8614)
- ObjectKind.Companion is the minion, not the chocobo buddy - upstream itself
  says "Begleiter" for the minion guide's search box, and Dalamud documents
  the kind as "a companion (minion)". It said 버디, which is the chocobo
- 방위, 손패 and 장판 have zero hits in the whole sheet - the last is player
  slang. They are now 방향 안내, 카드 and 범위
- The catalogue's HP row pointed at 9125, which is the chocobo racing stat
  block. The client's own label is row 232, "HP" - the word 체력 there is a
  chocobo attribute, and one site had already picked it up

The catalogue that was supposed to prevent guessing had 28 rows while the
translation used more than twice that many game words. The words were right -
the equipment slots match Addon 738-751 one for one - but the evidence was not
written down, and evidence that is not written down cannot be told apart from a
guess. It now holds 101 rows.

Two sites are left in the ternary on purpose.

- CounterConnector ("von"/"of") is read back by the mod itself.
  UIReaderService.TryParseSpokenProgress recognises a hunting-log row by
  splitting "3 von 48" into exactly three pieces and comparing the middle one
  to this constant. Korean puts the total first, so translating the word alone
  is not enough - Counter() and the parser have to move together, and that is a
  code change, not a translation
- "{name}: {distance}, {direction}." is byte-identical in German and English.
  A branch with two identical arms has nothing to translate. That is the second
  one found (AttributeValue is the other) and both are worth sending upstream

Word order moved where Korean needs it: ChatFromLine reads "{sender} {prefix}:
{message}", and counters read "{total} 중 {done}". Placeholder names are
untouched; the tool checks that the set is identical, so a dropped slot cannot
slip through.

German and English wording is byte-for-byte what it was. The tool only appends a
third argument; it never reads or rewrites the first two.

Build: 0 warnings, 0 errors against ClientStructs 7.55 and 7.51
Verified: DE/EN snapshot unchanged - 688 pairs; ko-apply round trip green
In-Game: not checked

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
